# ── 2026-05-04 (Spiking VTA / Posterior Tuberculum) ─────────────────────────

[2026-05-04] zebrav2/brain/vta.py
  NEW: Spiking VTA / posterior tuberculum — population-coded DA source
  - 40 RS-type Izhikevich neurons; i_tonic=6.0 pA → baseline DA ≈ 0.5
  - RPE phasic burst: +40 pA; reward omission pause: −30 pA (GABA)
  - LHb GABA-mediated suppression: −35 pA × lhb_rate (Matsumoto & Hikosaka 2007)
  - Amygdala chronic stress: −10 pA × amygdala_stress
  - IPN aversion feedback: 15 pA × ipn_da_feedback
  - Scale formula: da_raw = 0.4 + 10.0 × mean_rate (calibrated: baseline=0.492)
  - HPA cortisol suppression: da_raw *= hpa_suppression
  - phasic flag: rpe > 0.15 and I_rpe_phasic > 5.0
  - 20-substep spiking loop, noise σ=0.8 pA
  - References: Schultz et al. 1997; Rink & Wullimann 2001; Kastenhuber et al. 2010

[2026-05-04] zebrav2/brain/brain_v2.py
  FEAT: Wire SpikingVTA into neuromod pipeline
  - Import + instantiate self.vta = SpikingVTA(device)
  - VTA block runs after raphe/LC; reads nm['RPE'], hab_out['lhb_rate'],
    amygdala_alpha, hpa.da_suppression(), ipn_out['da_feedback']
  - Overrides neuromod.DA buffer (clamped 0–1)
  - Output keys: vta_da, vta_phasic, vta_rpe_ema
  - reset(): self.vta.reset()

